    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **268 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature by extending the existing owner-response mapping (the same mechanism that produces `displayName`), so initials are computed from the persisted entity and appear on all owner responses:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the property.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", ...)` expression plus a static `initials(Owner)` helper that returns the upper-cased first letters of the first and last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `\"J.S.\"`).\n\nThe `Cp07Tests.coreInitials` test (creates an owner with first name `John` / surname starting `Sur`, then GETs it and asserts `$.initials == \"J.S.\"`) passes, and nothing else regressed.",
